=== T1. Findings
G1: closed. S4 (LocalCommandBackend.complete) and S5 (cli._runtime) now fail
  the new test. S8 (the --message branch of cli.main) also fails it.
G2 (new, not blocking for this commit, but D2 waits for it): the interactive
  session is not exercised. S7 (a socket at the start of the interactive
  loop) and S6 (a socket in the /remember command branch) pass the full
  suite, 55 tests. The new test runs only "--message hello", which is a plain
  reply; no slash command and no interactive line runs under the audit hook.
  The interactive loop is how the owner uses NOVA, so D2 is not ticked.
  Suggested fix: a second test that patches builtins.input to return
  "/remember a", "/mem a", "/status", "hello", "/quit" in turn, runs
  cli.main(["--config", ...]) under record_socket_events(), and asserts
  exit 0 and no events. Show S6 and S7 failing in a scratch copy.
The fake runner is a child process; the audit hook sees only this Python
process. That limit is stated in the module docstring and still holds.

=== T2. Could not do / unsure of
Could not do: run on POSIX; this host is Windows, python 3.13.15.
Unsure of: whether other commands (/request, /confirm, /speak,
/propose-update) open sockets; they were not planted. The G2 test above would
cover them.

